1
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:53,020
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:55,950
[Episode 8]

3
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:56,700
One and a half catties.

4
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:57,880
Two catties!

5
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:58,290
Alright.

6
00:00:58,290 --> 00:00:59,680
Two yuan. Two yuan per portion.

7
00:01:00,390 --> 00:01:00,980
Just like this!

8
00:01:01,010 --> 00:01:02,250
He just gave a foreign currency note.

9
00:01:01,180 --> 00:01:03,680
[Paintwork] [Waxing] [Polishing]

10
00:01:06,790 --> 00:01:07,450
Two catties.

11
00:01:08,010 --> 00:01:08,780
Two catties.

12
00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:10,800
Come on, let's bag it.

13
00:01:15,430 --> 00:01:15,950
Alright.

14
00:01:15,970 --> 00:01:16,520
Here you are.

15
00:01:17,789 --> 00:01:18,980
Take care. Goodbye!

16
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:22,730
Big plums for sale!

17
00:01:22,870 --> 00:01:24,440
Come take a look!

18
00:01:25,039 --> 00:01:26,010
Big plums for sale!

19
00:01:27,390 --> 00:01:28,840
Come on in, quick.

20
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,120
Freezing cold out there.

21
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:36,979
You must be chilled to the bone.

22
00:01:37,979 --> 00:01:38,920
Don't bother to hide it!

23
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:40,710
I'm not conducting a search here.

24
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:41,470
You're not...

25
00:01:41,539 --> 00:01:42,400
This little girl...

26
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,500
Look after her for a while for me.

27
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,289
Your hands are ice-cold.

28
00:01:49,789 --> 00:01:50,700
Wh-What's up?

29
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:52,039
Not taking her with you today?

30
00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:55,400
The other day, Zhang from the photo studio
was saying,

31
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,810
"Who assigned Juan a police dog?

32
00:01:57,810 --> 00:01:58,780
She takes it everywhere.

33
00:01:58,780 --> 00:01:59,789
It doesn't run off or bark.

34
00:01:59,789 --> 00:02:01,080
How very obedient."

35
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:03,780
He can't even tell a human from a dog
with those eyes of his.

36
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:05,870
With such poor eyesight,
how can he take photos of others?

37
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:08,470
He must snap photos randomly then.

38
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:10,009
Look at your ears...

39
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,280
I'll pick her up at noon.

40
00:02:27,829 --> 00:02:28,610
Okay.

41
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:33,130
Why is this kid so clingy to you?

42
00:02:33,250 --> 00:02:35,180
People who don't know better would assume
she's your daughter.

43
00:02:35,410 --> 00:02:36,300
She takes after her mother.

44
00:02:36,810 --> 00:02:37,690
They're both like syrup—

45
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:39,280
you can't shake it off
once it sticks onto you.

46
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:39,840
Yeah.

47
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:40,800
She's good at pleasing others.

48
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:41,810
I can tell that.

49
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:46,900
It's a compliment.

50
00:02:47,430 --> 00:02:48,579
It means you're lovable.

51
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:50,470
How pretty you are.

52
00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:52,650
What a doll.

53
00:02:52,650 --> 00:02:53,530
Look at her little cheeks.

54
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:58,710
I'm heading to the crematorium in a bit.

55
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:03,930
You always say I'm superstitious.

56
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:05,670
As a materialist,

57
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:06,690
the crematorium—

58
00:03:06,690 --> 00:03:07,870
do you also fear that?

59
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:08,800
The crematorium.

60
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:12,000
Is it a proper place for children to be?

61
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,740
Li Dewu's funeral is today.

62
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:15,690
I have to show up.

63
00:03:22,310 --> 00:03:23,579
H-Has that missing hand

64
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:26,430
of his been retrieved yet?

65
00:03:28,210 --> 00:03:28,860
That's troubling.

66
00:03:35,750 --> 00:03:36,590
I performed a divination.

67
00:03:36,810 --> 00:03:37,870
Within a three-mile radius,

68
00:03:38,430 --> 00:03:39,579
in less than a week,

69
00:03:40,410 --> 00:03:41,280
it will surely be found.

70
00:03:41,910 --> 00:03:43,500
Come on, give it a rest.

71
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,520
You can actually predict that?

72
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:46,360
-You just don't believe it.
-What are the police for then?

73
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,230
Oh you. I really...

74
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:50,190
did put my heart into it. I did.

75
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:52,020
Well, the kid sometimes gets snacky.

76
00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:52,800
Buy her snacks later.

77
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,100
Y-You stop with it!

78
00:03:54,130 --> 00:03:55,020
This is complete nonsense.

79
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:56,470
How much could snacks
for a kid possibly cost?

80
00:03:56,470 --> 00:03:58,300
-Alright. Just take the money.
-This is so demeaning.

81
00:03:58,300 --> 00:03:58,930
Why refuse it?

82
00:03:58,930 --> 00:03:59,579
Better keep things separate.

83
00:03:59,579 --> 00:04:00,190
It's what discipline calls for.

84
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:01,630
How could you reject it?

85
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:02,210
You...

86
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:06,690
You really are a handful.

87
00:04:07,930 --> 00:04:08,910
Listen up.

88
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,910
If you dare pull tricks
and scam others again,

89
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:12,270
I'll arrest you one more time.

90
00:04:13,090 --> 00:04:14,080
Who's scamming others?

91
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:15,760
I perform divinations
using the Book of Changes.

92
00:04:15,970 --> 00:04:17,420
Then next time, perform a divination
for the kid

93
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:18,899
and find out
when her father will come get her.

94
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:20,220
Can...

95
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:22,810
Can you bring yourself
to let her father take her away?

96
00:04:24,950 --> 00:04:26,070
That must be a lie.

97
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:27,920
She even gave me money.

98
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:28,980
Seriously, what a day.

99
00:04:29,690 --> 00:04:31,550
Look, 20 cents, 50 cents, small bills...

100
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:39,480
Hey, little one.

101
00:04:43,370 --> 00:04:44,770
Looking at the drum, aren't you?

102
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:47,630
You like it?

103
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:49,620
Okay.

104
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,480
How about
a little performance for you, huh?

105
00:04:54,450 --> 00:04:56,500
I-I am actually a musician.

106
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:57,010
Let's do it.

107
00:04:59,159 --> 00:05:00,420
Clap your hands. A little chat first.

108
00:05:00,420 --> 00:05:01,480
A round of applause now.

109
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:03,860
Thanks for the support!

110
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:23,190
♪ Immortals, open your eyes,
keep watch, and take heed ♪

111
00:05:23,190 --> 00:05:27,300
♪ The Bridge of Despair is not far away ♪

112
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:35,040
[Funeral]

113
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:31,510
♪ A woman stands at the head
of the Bridge of Despair ♪

114
00:05:31,510 --> 00:05:35,130
♪ She's dressed in coarse hemp,
in clothes all torn and worn ♪

115
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,600
Have you heard?

116
00:05:43,810 --> 00:05:45,130
At Yuhong Square,

117
00:05:43,909 --> 00:05:47,520
[Funeral]

118
00:05:45,130 --> 00:05:46,600
a weasel spirit is claiming lives.

119
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:47,510
It's said

120
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:49,560
that it'll take three lives.

121
00:05:49,810 --> 00:05:50,800
Three?

122
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:51,770
Didn't Li Dewu

123
00:05:51,770 --> 00:05:53,060
die at that very square?

124
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:54,180
What now?

125
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:56,100
Even weasel immortals have become

126
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:56,990
bullies and bandits?

127
00:05:57,300 --> 00:05:58,180
Don't talk nonsense!

128
00:05:59,070 --> 00:06:01,190
The stories going around
are absolutely wild.

129
00:06:01,690 --> 00:06:03,730
Li Dewu lost his hand, didn't he?

130
00:06:03,930 --> 00:06:04,830
I heard

131
00:06:04,830 --> 00:06:06,450
it was bitten off him alive

132
00:06:06,450 --> 00:06:08,410
by an unknown creature.

133
00:06:08,690 --> 00:06:09,570
How terrifying!

134
00:06:09,570 --> 00:06:13,180
Family of the deceased, please enter.

135
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:17,590
[In deep mourning for Mr. Li Dewu]

136
00:06:14,190 --> 00:06:20,160
Time to send Mr. Li off
on his final journey.

137
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:25,800
The deceased has ascended
to the immortal realm.

138
00:06:27,370 --> 00:06:31,660
May his family accept our condolences.

139
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:39,450
Family members, perform the first bow

140
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:43,480
in memory of Mr. Li's profound grace.

141
00:06:44,190 --> 00:06:46,770
Perform the second bow

142
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:51,220
as you shed tears.

143
00:06:52,270 --> 00:06:54,980
Perform the third bow.

144
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:59,690
May Mr. Li's noble spirit prevail.

145
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:06,390
Family members, please
bid farewell to the deceased,

146
00:07:06,390 --> 00:07:10,740
and pay your respects in turn.

147
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:35,800
My son...

148
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:46,800
Thank you.

149
00:08:02,210 --> 00:08:03,370
[Police Badge]

150
00:08:02,290 --> 00:08:03,210
My name is Liu Juan,

151
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:06,010
a police officer
of Yuhong Square Police Station.

152
00:08:07,610 --> 00:08:08,470
Anything wrong, sir?

153
00:08:09,970 --> 00:08:11,250
You have something to say, don't you?

154
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:11,800
No rush.

155
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:12,510
Take your time.

156
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:15,870
You can blink, right?

157
00:08:16,530 --> 00:08:17,210
How about this?

158
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:18,930
I'll ask you questions.

159
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:21,080
If your answer is yes,

160
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,200
blink once.

161
00:08:22,950 --> 00:08:24,730
If not, blink twice.

162
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:26,320
I'll get started now.

163
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:30,950
Did your son make an enemy
when he was alive?

164
00:08:32,409 --> 00:08:33,700
He did, right?

165
00:08:34,210 --> 00:08:34,789
Is this person

166
00:08:34,789 --> 00:08:36,240
in Tiecheng right now?

167
00:08:40,010 --> 00:08:41,360
How old is he?

168
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,299
Male or female?

169
00:08:48,390 --> 00:08:49,010
I'm sorry, sir.

170
00:08:49,010 --> 00:08:50,890
Should've organized my questions.

171
00:08:50,890 --> 00:08:51,630
No need to rush.

172
00:08:51,630 --> 00:08:52,690
Take it easy, sir.

173
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:54,220
Officer.

174
00:08:54,630 --> 00:08:56,250
My dad just survived a stroke.

175
00:08:56,250 --> 00:08:57,480
He can't take any shocks.

176
00:08:58,340 --> 00:08:59,510
I know everything about my husband.

177
00:08:59,510 --> 00:09:00,100
You can ask me instead.

178
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:00,740
Okay.

179
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:01,630
Sorry for that.

180
00:09:01,630 --> 00:09:03,020
My condolences, sir.

181
00:09:05,290 --> 00:09:06,520
You're Officer Liu, right?

182
00:09:06,570 --> 00:09:07,630
That's too much of a title.

183
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:08,410
I'm merely a beat cop.

184
00:09:08,410 --> 00:09:09,630
Just call me Juan.

185
00:09:09,670 --> 00:09:12,010
Okay. How is it going?
Any updates on the case?

186
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:14,770
This is so odd.

187
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:16,480
A man's hand is not a bear paw.

188
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:17,940
It can't be cooked or used as medicine.

189
00:09:18,410 --> 00:09:19,700
Why would anyone want that?

190
00:09:20,290 --> 00:09:21,200
How did it end up...

191
00:09:23,340 --> 00:09:25,440
-His body is not complete!
-I'll attend to that.

192
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:25,910
Go ahead.

193
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:29,630
How is my son supposed
to enter the afterlife?

194
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:14,130
You did it, right?

195
00:10:30,910 --> 00:10:32,760
Stop the fuss, or I'll kill you.

196
00:10:32,790 --> 00:10:34,320
My poor son...

197
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:35,670
Ma'am, ma'am!

198
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:41,690
-My poor son...
-Careful.

199
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:43,070
Ma'am, ma'am!

200
00:10:48,140 --> 00:10:49,090
Wait a minute. Come here.

201
00:10:50,450 --> 00:10:51,760
Hold on! I need a word with you.

202
00:10:53,390 --> 00:10:54,250
What is it, Officer Liu?

203
00:10:54,630 --> 00:10:56,230
Last time you said your boss...

204
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:57,470
You mean Boss Wu.

205
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:59,820
On the day of his passing,
Boss Wu went to his usual hair salon

206
00:11:00,090 --> 00:11:02,440
and asked you to pick him up
at Yuhong Square at night.

207
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:03,860
Exactly.

208
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:04,860
What time?

209
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:06,050
Ten o'clock.

210
00:11:07,170 --> 00:11:07,930
Are you sure?

211
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:09,220
Yes, I'm sure.

212
00:11:09,770 --> 00:11:10,790
You've been here for a while.

213
00:11:10,790 --> 00:11:11,870
Have you noticed anyone

214
00:11:12,010 --> 00:11:13,460
acting suspiciously?

215
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:15,860
No, no one.

216
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:17,500
What are you trying to say?

217
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:18,890
Are you suggesting that Boss Wu

218
00:11:18,890 --> 00:11:19,750
was murdered?

219
00:11:19,750 --> 00:11:20,960
I didn't say that.

220
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:23,250
I just can't figure it out.

221
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:25,340
Look, he just stumbled.

222
00:11:26,290 --> 00:11:28,030
How did he end up losing a hand?

223
00:11:47,750 --> 00:11:49,180
I-I really have to go.

224
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:50,030
Off you go.

225
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:51,650
If you recall anything,

226
00:11:51,650 --> 00:11:52,540
do let me know.

227
00:12:50,510 --> 00:12:51,100
Eyes on the road.

228
00:12:51,810 --> 00:12:52,950
Drive carefully.

229
00:12:55,490 --> 00:12:58,670
[Two months ago]

230
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:35,280
Mrs. Li.

231
00:14:10,770 --> 00:14:11,550
It hurts, right?

232
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:16,210
Try getting five stitches on your head.

233
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:26,620
You sent him to the hair salon?

234
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,510
How come he's not dead
from all that wild oats-sewing?

235
00:14:45,470 --> 00:14:46,390
Turn right.

236
00:14:48,670 --> 00:14:49,880
[Turn right to exit the city]

237
00:14:55,570 --> 00:14:56,400
Turn right!

238
00:14:57,900 --> 00:15:01,230
[Turn right to exit the city]

239
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:26,890
Boss Wu is paging me.

240
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:34,960
Mrs. Li.

241
00:15:38,530 --> 00:15:39,270
No.

242
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:41,340
Hong.

243
00:15:43,890 --> 00:15:44,600
Be good.

244
00:15:45,030 --> 00:15:45,720
I'll take you

245
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:46,840
wherever you want to

246
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,390
after picking up Boss Wu, alright?

247
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:51,730
As long as I get to leave Tiecheng,

248
00:15:52,130 --> 00:15:53,240
I'll happy anywhere.

249
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:54,770
What?

250
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:55,890
What did you say?

251
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:57,440
Are you okay?

252
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:58,840
What's wrong with you?

253
00:16:00,390 --> 00:16:01,270
Come on, Hong,

254
00:16:01,270 --> 00:16:02,980
let's not do this, okay?

255
00:16:02,980 --> 00:16:04,120
If you suddenly run away from home,

256
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:06,150
how am I supposed to explain it
to Boss Wu?

257
00:16:06,150 --> 00:16:07,290
What's there explain?

258
00:16:07,290 --> 00:16:08,390
Just leave with me!

259
00:16:10,030 --> 00:16:11,320
You must be kidding.

260
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:12,770
That'll make me a kidnapper, won't it?

261
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:14,130
If I take Boss Wu's wife away

262
00:16:14,130 --> 00:16:15,280
while driving his car,

263
00:16:15,460 --> 00:16:17,530
I'll be caught before leaving Tiecheng.

264
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:19,220
No, don't do this!

265
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:19,910
You are not to make a U-turn!

266
00:16:19,910 --> 00:16:20,390
L-Let go of my arm!

267
00:16:20,390 --> 00:16:20,840
No U-turn!

268
00:16:21,270 --> 00:16:22,100
A truck! There's a truck!

269
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:33,700
Are you okay?

270
00:16:48,150 --> 00:16:50,270
I don't want to die in that house.

271
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,550
Right, I know.

272
00:16:58,440 --> 00:16:59,220
Boss Wu

273
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:00,600
does have a bad temper.

274
00:17:01,250 --> 00:17:03,130
But I think you're fine this time.

275
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,030
Look, none of your bones got fractured.

276
00:17:13,660 --> 00:17:15,109
You promised to take me away.

277
00:17:19,180 --> 00:17:21,109
I didn't say it would be today.

278
00:17:21,130 --> 00:17:22,290
It has to be today!

279
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:26,420
I don't have my ID with me.
